        "original_id": "a64d83f3-4bcc-5283-a88c-bdb55a90194f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sidney Olcott, Denis Villeneuve, Gene Gauntier\n- Works: From the Manger to the Cross, August 32nd on Earth, Maelström, Polytechnique, Incendies, Enemy\n- Roles: film producer, director, actor, screenwriter, writer\n- Awards: Canadian Screen Award, Genie Award\n\nFacts:\n- Sidney Olcott was born on September 20, 1872, and he was a Canadian-born film producer, director, actor, and screenwriter.\n- From the Manger to the Cross was directed by Sidney Olcott, who also appeared in the film.\n- Gene Gauntier wrote the script for From the Manger to the Cross and portrayed the Virgin Mary in the film.\n- Denis Villeneuve was born on October 3, 1967, and he is a French Canadian film director and writer.\n- August 32nd on Earth, also known by the French title Un 32 août sur terre and as 32nd Day of August on Earth, is a 1998 Canadian drama film directed by Denis Villeneuve.\n- Denis Villeneuve received the Canadian Screen Award, formerly called the Genie Award, for Best Direction for Maelström in 2001, Polytechnique in 2010, Incendies in 2011, and Enemy in 2013.\n- Sidney Olcott died on December 16, 1949.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f3c216b3-d844-56f3-b804-7fa84ef038b4",
        "text": "Page: Sidney Olcott. Sentence: Sidney Olcott (September 20, 1872 – December 16, 1949) was a Canadian-born film producer, director, actor and screenwriter.\nPage: Denis Villeneuve. Sentence: Denis Villeneuve (] ; born October 3, 1967) is a French Canadian film director and writer.\nPage: Denis Villeneuve. Sentence: He is a four-time recipient of the Canadian Screen Award (formerly Genie Award) for Best Direction, for \"Maelström\" in 2001, \"Polytechnique\" in 2010, \"Incendies\" in 2011, and \"Enemy\" in 2013.\nPage: From the Manger to the Cross. Sentence: Directed by Sidney Olcott who also appeared in the film, actress and screenwriter Gene Gauntier wrote the script and portrayed the Virgin Mary.\nPage: August 32nd on Earth. Sentence: August 32nd on Earth (French: Un 32 août sur terre , and also known as \"32nd Day of August on Earth\") is a 1998 Canadian drama film directed by Denis Villeneuve.",
